# The build context is what a compromised or careless build could publish, so it
# holds what the build needs and nothing else.
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT here. It is what stamps vcs.revision, vcs.time and
# vcs.modified into the binary, and that build info is the provenance this agent
# reads off customer workloads — an image of ours that could not answer the same
# question would be the one thing we tell customers to look for (ADR 0085).

# Private notes. Nothing in this file may reach a committed artifact, and a
# build context is an artifact the moment a cache or an intermediate stage is
# exported (CLAUDE.md).
CONTEXT.md

# Build output and run logs: never inputs, sometimes large.
bin/
test/e2e/logs/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
